# Unlocking a Room's door is a special action (CR 709.5e, 116.2m), not an ability of the Room, so an effect that takes all
# abilities cannot take it. Opalescence makes Unholy Annex a creature, and Humility takes all its abilities: Annex's end
# step ability is gone (no card drawn and no life lost at the end of turns 5 and 7), yet the right door is still offered
# and unlocked for its {3}{B}{B}. The Room has no abilities once it is unlocked either, so Ritual Chamber's "when you
# unlock this door" does not trigger (CR 603.2): no Demon. Under Humility the Room is a 1/1, its name both doors' and its
# mana value 8 (CR 709.5, 709.4b).

